        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "test(tui): lock dunder markdown rendering",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nCloses #90769. Prevents regressions where narrow TUI Markdown wrapping splits Python dunder and underscore identifiers inside fenced or inline code.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nCurrent `main` upgraded `@earendil-works/pi-tui` from 0.78.0 to 0.80.3 in #99949. Direct dependency inspection and current-main rendering now show that upstream keeps `__name__`, `__main__`, `is_palindrome`, and `__init__` intact while respecting the terminal width.\n\nThe original PR's 135-line production patch wrapped pi-tui's private `Markdown.renderToken` method. That is no longer the best fix: it duplicates the current upstream renderer and creates a private dependency seam. This rewrite removes the monkey patch entirely and keeps only focused regression coverage against the public `HyperlinkMarkdown` behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo new runtime path. The corrected behavior already exists on current `main`; this PR locks it in so future dependency or wrapper changes cannot silently corrupt displayed code identifiers.\n\nContributor credit is preserved for @zhangguiping-xydt, whose report, proof, and original PR supplied the regression cases.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Current-main render at width 12 moves `__name__` and `__main__` to fitting lines without splitting either identifier; fenced `is_palindrome` and inline `__init__` also remain intact.\n- `OPENCLAW_HEAVY_CHECK_LOCK_SCOPE=worktree node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/tui/components/hyperlink-markdown.test.ts src/tui/components/chat-log.test.ts src/tui/tui-formatters.test.ts src/tui/theme/theme.test.ts` — 4 files, 98 tests passed.\n- `git diff --cached --check` — passed before commit.\n- Fresh autoreview found one test-boundary gap; the test was tightened to force the dunder token across a real width boundary. Second autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings (0.98 confidence).\n\n## Scope\n\nTest-only. No config, protocol, provider, auth, persistence, or tool-execution behavior changed. No changelog entry required.\n\n## AI Assistance\n\nAI-assisted maintainer rewrite and review.\n",
